i20260217-v6","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-3417-3","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-391529-i20260217","date":"2026-02-17","original_code":"746.3417(3)","severity":"medium_high","severity_label":"Medium-high risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2026-03-05","finding":"Children Handwashing After Toileting or Diapering: A caregiver failed to wash a child's hands immediately following a diaper change.","topic":"sanitation","source_record_id":"1026489209","violation_type_title":"Children Handwashing After Toileting or Diapering (26 TAC §746.3417(3))","topic_label":"Sanitation & hygiene"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-391529-i20260217-v7","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-3701","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-391529-i20260217","date":"2026-02-17","original_code":"746.3701","severity":"medium_high","severity_label":"Medium-high risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2026-03-05","finding":"Safety - Areas Free From Hazards: The following hazards were observed during the inspection:     *A bottle of Lysol Gel was observed on the back of a toilet in one of the children s restrooms, posing a potential safety hazard as it was within their reach.  (Note:  The caregiver removed the chemical during the inspection).       *There was a bag of potting soil observed on the playground accessible to children.  (Note:  The bag of potting soil was removed during the inspections).  .      *There were several broken toys observed on the playground accessible to children.  (Note:  The broken toys were discarded during the inspection).     *The padding around the splash pad is damaged leaving the concrete foundation exposed and creating a tripping hazard for children.","topic":"safety","source_record_id":"1026248658","violation_type_title":"Safety - Areas Free From Hazards (26 TAC §746.3701)","topic_label":"Safety hazards"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-391529-i20260217-v8","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-2428","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-391529-i20260217","date":"2026-02-17","original_code"